{"steps":[{"step":"request_human","verdict":"valid","why":"The policy states that the agent should say it can help and try first, and counting the requests is what transfer_on_fourth_request needs.","clauses":[{"clause":"Count each request for a human","kind":"derived","source":"Policy: 'If the user asks for a human agent 4 times, then you may invoke the transfer_to_human_agents tool' can only be applied if the requests are counted."}]},{"step":"transfer_on_fourth_request","verdict":"valid","why":"The 4-request transfer is in the policy, and the reason choice follows doc 042's highest-tier rule with its fraud row.","clauses":[{"clause":"fraud_or_security_concern when fraud or unauthorized transactions are involved","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 042 says to select from the highest tier that applies. Its tier-1 row fraud_or_security_concern names 'unauthorized transactions'."}]},{"step":"from_review_handoff","verdict":"valid","why":"The policy states that verification happens only once per conversation, and re-reading only missing records follows from that.","clauses":[{"clause":"re-read a record only if it is missing","kind":"derived","source":"Policy 'No need to verify more than once in a single conversation'. Records already read in the conversation are the same records."}]},{"step":"from_pin_lock_handoff","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 041 states that a dispute is filed when unauthorized transactions are found, and the unbounded suspicious period is handled by asking the customer.","clauses":[{"clause":"show transactions from the earliest declined attempt to now; dispute only the ones they deny","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 041 Step 6.1 says to check for successful unauthorized transactions during the suspicious period, and Step 2 names the declined types. The period has no bounds, so the window only orders what is shown and the customer says which are not theirs."},{"clause":"fraud category by channel; card_in_possession and pin_compromised asked","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 gives the fraud split by channel and gives the card_in_possession and pin_compromised questions, including 'unknown': Customer unsure."}]},{"step":"pin_lock_no_unauthorized_no_dispute","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 041 Step 6.3 states the explanation and the three options when no unauthorized transaction is found.","clauses":[{"clause":"file nothing for that card","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 041 6.2 files a dispute only 'If unauthorized transactions found'. 6.3 gives explanation and options instead."}]},{"step":"pin_lock_each_withdrawal","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 makes transaction_id the ID of the single transaction being disputed, so each denied transaction gets its own dispute.","clauses":[{"clause":"one dispute per transaction_id, never one for the total","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says transaction_id is 'ID of the transaction being disputed', one ID per filing. Doc 041 says 'File dispute' for each unauthorized transaction found."}]},{"step":"greet","verdict":"valid","why":"The policy requires verification with 2 of the 4 values before a dispute is filed.","clauses":[]},{"step":"lookup_user","verdict":"valid","why":"These are the read tools in the policy's verification procedure, and the name lookup is case sensitive per its description.","clauses":[]},{"step":"check_identity","verdict":"valid","why":"The policy states 2-of-4 verification and no leaking before verification.","clauses":[{"clause":"If they still do not match after you ask again, say you cannot verify them, and stop","kind":"kept","source":"The policy requires verification before account access but sets no retry count. The clause forbids proceeding unverified, and no passage overrules it."}]},{"step":"get_time","verdict":"valid","why":"The policy states that get_current_time must be used for the current time.","clauses":[]},{"step":"log_verification","verdict":"valid","why":"The policy states that the verification must be logged after it succeeds.","clauses":[]},{"step":"one_dispute_at_a_time","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 performs the card action after all disputes and counts limits per account, and the policy verifies once.","clauses":[{"clause":"Ask the written-statement question once","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 asks to use 'this conversation as your written statement'. One agreement covers the whole conversation."}]},{"step":"get_accounts","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 009 names the tool, and doc 005 lists the products in each tier.","clauses":[{"clause":"The class field is not the tier","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 009 lists account_type and account_class as fields. The order_debit_card_5739 error uses class as checking vs savings ('is a {class} account'), and doc 005 gives tiers by product name."}]},{"step":"get_cards","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 028 names the tool and the card_number_last_4 field.","clauses":[]},{"step":"get_transactions","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 says to find the transaction with get_bank_account_transactions_9173.","clauses":[]},{"step":"match_failed","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 requires the transaction_id from the transaction records, so a transaction that is not in the records cannot be filed.","clauses":[{"clause":"Never file a dispute for a transaction that is not in the records","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says transaction_id is to be found with get_bank_account_transactions_9173. With no record there is no ID."}]},{"step":"amount_differs_from_record","verdict":"valid","why":"The recorded transaction is what is disputed, and doc 031 defines incorrect_amount as a difference, so the amounts follow; whether to file is the customer's choice.","clauses":[{"clause":"whole-charge dispute uses the recorded charge; incorrect_amount uses recorded minus expected","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 defines disputed_amount as 'The dollar amount being disputed' and transaction_id as the recorded transaction. Doc 032 says 'Maximum: The full transaction amount'. incorrect_amount means 'Charged different amount than expected', so the difference is what is in dispute."},{"clause":"A dispute that is not filed sets no card action","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 performs the card action 'after filing all disputes' across those disputes."}]},{"step":"pick_earliest_duplicate","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states that the earliest duplicate is disputed.","clauses":[{"clause":"for the amount of one charge","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 duplicate_charge is 'Same transaction charged multiple times', and the earliest one transaction is disputed. Doc 032 caps the dispute at the full transaction amount."}]},{"step":"get_dispute_status","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 names the tool.","clauses":[]},{"step":"count_open_disputes","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 speaks of 'open disputes' across in-progress statuses, and its resolved, reversed and closed statuses are terminal.","clauses":[{"clause":"Count OPEN, PENDING_DOCUMENTATION, UNDER_REVIEW, PROVISIONAL_CREDIT_ISSUED as open","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035 'check the status of open disputes'. Its status list describes these four as investigation ongoing or under review, and the RESOLVED_*, PROVISIONAL_REVERSED and CLOSED_NO_RESPONSE statuses as final. Doc 031 counts limits per account_id."}]},{"step":"timeline_escalation","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 states both timelines and the escalation, doc 032 decides which categories require credit, and the policy requires asking before transfer.","clauses":[{"clause":"credit timeline checked only for the doc 032 REQUIRED categories","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035 says credit 'should be issued within 10 days (20 for new accounts)'. Doc 032 lists the categories where credit is required and those where it is not."},{"clause":"investigation timeline not checked for UNDER_REVIEW or resolved/closed","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035 says UNDER_REVIEW means 'Investigation complete', and resolved and closed statuses are final."}]},{"step":"check_prefiling","verdict":"valid","why":"Each check is a doc 031 pre-filing requirement, with tiers from doc 005.","clauses":[]},{"step":"explain_limit_and_choose","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 sets the per-account limit and the 60-day rule; the order of filing is asked.","clauses":[{"clause":"rest can be filed once existing disputes close, within 60 days","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says the limit counts open disputes, so a closed one frees a slot. The 60-day age rule still applies at filing."}]},{"step":"gather_details","verdict":"valid","why":"Each question is one doc 031 asks for a tool argument or for its ATM pre-filing requirement.","clauses":[]},{"step":"pin_compromised_unsure","verdict":"valid","why":"This is doc 031's own value list for pin_compromised.","clauses":[]},{"step":"type_from_customer_report","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 says the transaction type is determined from the user's circumstances; the agent asks again instead of guessing.","clauses":[]},{"step":"discovery_date_from_alert","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 defines discovery_date as the date the customer first noticed the issue.","clauses":[]},{"step":"statement_date","verdict":"valid","why":"The liability tiers are counted from the statement, and no tool returns statement dates, so the customer is asked.","clauses":[{"clause":"A statement they were reviewing is dated on or before their discovery_date","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says discovery_date is the date first noticed. A statement being read when it was noticed already existed on that date."}]},{"step":"liability_disclosure","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the disclosure before filing and its three tiers.","clauses":[]},{"step":"late_report_liability","verdict":"valid","why":"The $500 tier and the credit offset are stated, and the bounds follow from the statement showing the transaction.","clauses":[{"clause":"a report within 60 days (or 2 business days) of the transaction is within that time of the statement","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 032 refers to 'the statement date showing the transaction'. A statement that shows a transaction is dated on or after it, so the time to the report is no longer than from the transaction."},{"clause":"a report more than 2 business days after the reviewed statement's date bound is past the 2-business-day window","kind":"derived","source":"statement_date: the reviewed statement is dated on or before discovery_date. Doc 031 sets the 2-business-day tier from the statement."}]},{"step":"choose_category","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 lists the categories and states the fraud split.","clauses":[]},{"step":"incorrect_amount_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"The category, card action and no-credit-required status are stated, and the amount is the difference.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount = posted charge minus expected amount","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 defines disputed_amount as 'The dollar amount being disputed' and incorrect_amount as 'Charged different amount than expected', so the amount in dispute is the difference."}]},{"step":"goods_not_received_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"The category, mapping, merchant question and credit status are stated, and the amount is the payment for the missing item.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount is the recorded amount paid for the item","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says the category is 'Paid but never received', so the payment is what is disputed. Doc 032 says 'Maximum: The full transaction amount'."}]},{"step":"p2p_fraud_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 names person_to_person, and its two-way fraud split puts a non-physical transfer in card_not_present_fraud.","clauses":[{"clause":"card_not_present_fraud for a P2P transfer","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: card_present_fraud is for 'in-store/physical transactions' when 'card was physically present', and card_not_present_fraud is for online/phone. A P2P transfer (EveryonePay) is not in-store or physical card use, so it falls in the other value. If the customer reports physical use, the customer is asked."}]},{"step":"in_person_fraud_with_card_held","verdict":"valid","why":"Each value is from doc 031's lists and its mapping.","clauses":[]},{"step":"recurring_charge_branch","verdict":"rewrite","why":"The block tool works only on an ACTIVE card, so 'a card that stays open' reads past the tool's own description for a FROZEN card.","clauses":[{"clause":"run block_recurring_payments on a card that stays open","kind":"unsupported","source":"The set_debit_card_recurring_block_7382 description says 'Card must be ACTIVE'. A FROZEN card stays open but cannot take the block."}],"rewrite":{"id":"recurring_charge_branch","by":"model","do":"For a subscription charged after it was cancelled:
- dispute_category recurring_charge_after_cancellation; its card_action maps to keep_active;
- transaction_type recurring_payment;
- contacted_merchant as the customer says.
Provisional credit is not required for this category, though it may be offered at discretion. If the customer wants future recurring charges stopped and the card is ACTIVE after the card actions, run block_recurring_payments after the disputes. If the card is closed, tell them recurring payments linked to it must be updated instead. If the card is not ACTIVE for another reason (for example FROZEN), tell them the block can only be set on an ACTIVE card.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["gather_details","get_transactions"],"after":["choose_category"],"if":"the customer was charged for a subscription or membership after cancelling it","quote":"For recurring charge disputes, the dispute_category should be 'recurring_charge_after_cancellation'.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_034","basis":[{"clause":"category","quote":"For recurring charge disputes, the dispute_category should be 'recurring_charge_after_cancellation'.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_034"},{"clause":"card_action keep_active","quote":"'recurring_charge_after_cancellation' → 'keep_active'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"transaction_type recurring_payment","quote":"'recurring_payment': Subscription or automatic payment","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"merchant contact","quote":"Ask: "Have you attempted to resolve this directly with the merchant?" Required for non-fraud disputes.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"provisional credit not required, may be offered","quote":"**Provisional Credit is NOT REQUIRED (but may be offered at discretion) when:**","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_032"},{"clause":"block after the dispute, if wanted","quote":"Then set up the recurring block for future protection","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_034"},{"clause":"block only on an ACTIVE card","quote":"Error: Cannot update recurring block settings for a card with status '{card_status}'. Card must be ACTIVE.","doc":"set_debit_card_recurring_block_7382"},{"clause":"closed card: update recurring payments","quote":"Any recurring payments linked to this card will need to be updated with new payment information","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"}]}},{"step":"lost_card_fraud_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"The fraud split, close reasons and cross-product trigger are stated, and card_in_possession false follows from a lost or stolen card.","clauses":[{"clause":"card_in_possession false","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 asks whether the customer still has the physical card. A card reported lost or stolen is not in the customer's possession."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_journal","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states each instruction for a Rho-Bank cash discrepancy.","clauses":[]},{"step":"rho_atm_amount_check","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 says the journal record is pulled from the account transactions, and the confirmed amount is the difference.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount = recorded amount minus cash received","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says the disputed_amount is the dollar amount disputed, and atm_cash_discrepancy is 'dispensed wrong amount', so the amount in dispute is the shortfall."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_not_validated","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states the claim may still be filed, which leaves filing to the customer, and the values come from doc 031.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount = amount requested minus cash received","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 defines the field as the dollar amount disputed. The customer's claim is the requested amount that was not dispensed, so the customer confirms the figure."}]},{"step":"atm_deposit_images","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states the tool, the comparison and the 45-day timeline.","clauses":[]},{"step":"deposit_compare","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the category, type and mapping, and the amount is the uncredited part.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount = amount deposited minus amount credited","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says atm_deposit_not_credited is 'deposit not reflected in account', and disputed_amount is the dollar amount disputed, so it is the part not reflected."}]},{"step":"third_party_atm_info","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states the chargeback, the 90 days and the credit for cash disputes, and doc 032 names atm_deposit_not_credited as not requiring credit.","clauses":[{"clause":"for atm_deposit_not_credited, do not say credit is required","kind":"derived","source":"Reading rule 3: doc 032 names 'atm_deposit_not_credited' under NOT REQUIRED. Doc 033's third-party line reaches deposits only through its heading."}]},{"step":"atm_affidavit_info","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 states each item for ATM cash discrepancies over $200.","clauses":[]},{"step":"recommend_police_report","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"police_report_incident_total","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 036 recommends a police report for any suspected fraud, especially over $500, and the tool requires the boolean.","clauses":[{"clause":"ask and recommend for an incident total over $500","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 036 says 'For suspected fraud, we recommend also filing a police report, especially for amounts over $500.' The tool requires police_report_filed, so it is asked."}]},{"step":"police_report_question_under_500","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 036 states the recommendation, and the required boolean is asked.","clauses":[]},{"step":"written_statement","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the question.","clauses":[]},{"step":"written_statement_reuse","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 offers 'this conversation' as the statement, so one agreement covers every later dispute in it.","clauses":[{"clause":"pass true for each later dispute","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'We can use this conversation as your written statement if you agree'. The same conversation covers every dispute filed in it."}]},{"step":"decide_provisional_credit","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 032 states the REQUIRED and NOT REQUIRED lists, and doc 033 names the ATM cases.","clauses":[{"clause":"a transaction no more than 60 days old meets condition 1","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 sets the 60-day age rule. Doc 032 counts from 'the statement date showing the transaction', which is on or after the transaction."},{"clause":"merchant item applies to unauthorized_transaction","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says unauthorized_transaction is used 'only when fraud is NOT suspected', so it is a non-fraud dispute under doc 032 item 2."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_confirmed_provisional","verdict":"rewrite","why":"Doc 033 names the confirmed Rho-Bank cash discrepancy and issues credit immediately, so withholding it on doc 032's general conditions follows the broader passage.","clauses":[{"clause":"Conditions 1, 3 and 4 must still hold","kind":"unsupported","source":"Reading rule 3: doc 033 says 'If discrepancy confirmed, provisional credit is issued immediately' for this case. Doc 032's conditions reach it only through its category list. The step already sets aside doc 032's merchant item on the same ground."}],"rewrite":{"id":"rho_atm_confirmed_provisional","by":"model","do":"A Rho-Bank ATM cash discrepancy confirmed by rho_atm_amount_check gets provisional_credit_eligible true. Doc 033 names this case, so doc 032's conditions and NOT REQUIRED items (merchant contact included) do not withhold it. Tell the customer the credit is issued immediately after filing.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["rho_atm_amount_check","get_accounts","get_time","written_statement"],"after":["decide_provisional_credit"],"if":"dispute_category is atm_cash_discrepancy at a Rho-Bank ATM AND the discrepancy was confirmed against the record","quote":"If discrepancy confirmed, provisional credit is issued immediately (no waiting period)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033","basis":[{"clause":"eligible true, issued immediately","quote":"If discrepancy confirmed, provisional credit is issued immediately (no waiting period)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"},{"clause":"journal from the transactions","quote":"View recent transactions on the corresponding checking accounts to pull ATM journal records for the transaction","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"}]}},{"step":"decide_parameters","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the card_action mapping, and the ATM amount is the shortfall.","clauses":[{"clause":"ATM cash discrepancy: recorded withdrawal minus cash received","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says atm_cash_discrepancy is 'dispensed wrong amount or no cash', and disputed_amount is the dollar amount disputed, so it is the difference (all of it when no cash came out)."}]},{"step":"file_dispute","verdict":"rewrite","why":"customer_max_liability_amount takes one of doc 031's tier values, and the 'lesser of tier and amount' arithmetic is stated by no passage.","clauses":[{"clause":"customer_max_liability_amount: the lesser of $50 and the amount, the lesser of $500 and the amount, or -1","kind":"unsupported","source":"Reading rule 1: doc 031 lists the values $50, $500 and unlimited, and the tool gives -1 for unlimited. The tool description says the value is 'based on ... reporting timing rules and the disputed amount' without saying how, which states no arithmetic."},{"clause":"disputed_amount per category from the records","kind":"derived","source":"See amount_differs_from_record, decide_parameters and deposit_compare."}],"rewrite":{"id":"file_dispute","by":"model","do":"Unlock file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281 once, then file each allowed dispute separately.
- If a reply says the dispute may already exist, do not call again for it; tell the customer.
- If a reply names a missing or invalid parameter, ask for or re-read that value, then file again.
- If filing still fails, tell the customer it was not filed (transfer_if_needed).","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281","transaction_id":"the transaction id from records (the earliest for duplicates)","account_id":"the linked checking account id","card_id":"the debit card id","user_id":"the verified user's id","dispute_category":"the category decided","transaction_date":"MM/DD/YYYY from records","discovery_date":"MM/DD/YYYY the customer gave (the get_current_time date if 'today')","disputed_amount":"from the records: the whole recorded charge for a whole-charge dispute (one charge for a duplicate); for incorrect_amount, the confirmed difference; for an ATM cash discrepancy, the recorded withdrawal minus the cash received; for atm_deposit_not_credited, the amount deposited minus the amount credited (deposit_compare)","transaction_type":"the type decided","card_in_possession":"the customer's answer","pin_compromised":"yes_shared | yes_observed | no | unknown","contacted_merchant":"the customer's answer","police_report_filed":"the customer's answer (ask if not yet asked)","written_statement_provided":"true if the customer agreed","provisional_credit_eligible":"from decide_provisional_credit / rho_atm_confirmed_provisional","card_action":"from that category's mapping","customer_max_liability_amount":"the doc 031 tier counted from the statement showing the transaction (late_report_liability): 50 if reported within 2 business days, 500 if within 60 days, -1 if after 60 days (unlimited)"},"lookup":["check_prefiling","decide_parameters"],"after":["decide_parameters"],"if":"the dispute passes the pre-filing rules and fits within the open-dispute limit, and the customer did not drop it (amount_differs_from_record, rho_atm_not_validated, deposit_compare)","quote":"**Tool: file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281**","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"tool to call","quote":"**Tool: file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281**","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"provisional_credit_eligible","quote":"Agent must determine based on Debit Card Provisional Credit Guidelines.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"confirmed Rho-Bank ATM","quote":"If discrepancy confirmed, provisional credit is issued immediately (no waiting period)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"},{"clause":"third-party ATM","quote":"Provisional credit is still required within 10 business days","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"},{"clause":"disputed amount","quote":"The dollar amount being disputed.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"whole-charge amount from the record","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"deposit category","quote":"'atm_deposit_not_credited': ATM deposit not reflected in account","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"liability $50","quote":"Reported within 2 business days of statement: Maximum liability $50","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"liability $500","quote":"Reported within 60 days of statement: Maximum liability $500","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"liability unlimited","quote":"Reported after 60 days: Unlimited liability - customer may not recover funds","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"-1 for unlimited","quote":"Use -1 for unlimited liability.","doc":"file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281"},{"clause":"already-filed reply, required booleans, retry on a named error","source":"none","why":"From the file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281 tool description and its replies."}]}},{"step":"decide_card_action","verdict":"rewrite","why":"Doc 041 closes a cannot-unlock PIN-locked card when unauthorized transactions are found, so conditioning that closure on a filed dispute borrows doc 031's broader rule against the passage that names the case.","clauses":[{"clause":"most severe action among filed disputes, performed once","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes, use the MOST SEVERE action', with its severity order."},{"clause":"PIN lock card closes only 'with at least one denied transaction filed'","kind":"unsupported","source":"Reading rules 2 and 3: doc 041 6.2 says 'If unauthorized transactions found: File dispute, close card, order replacement'. The closure turns on found, which is the customer's denial, not on filing. Doc 031's after-filing rule reaches the case only generally."}],"rewrite":{"id":"decide_card_action","by":"model","do":"After all disputes are filed, take each card's most severe card_action among its filed disputes (close_and_reissue > freeze_pending_investigation > keep_active) and perform it once. For keep_active, do nothing. For a card that came from the PIN lock investigation's cannot-unlock path on which the customer denied at least one successful transaction, the card's action is close_and_reissue (close the card, then order_replacement), whatever its disputes' categories map to and even if a denied transaction could not be filed. Each dispute still records its own category's card_action.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["decide_parameters","file_dispute","get_cards"],"after":["file_dispute"],"if":"at least one dispute was filed, or the card came from the PIN lock cannot-unlock path and the customer denied at least one successful transaction on it","quote":"However, when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes, use the MOST SEVERE action across all disputes.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"most severe action after all disputes","quote":"However, when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes, use the MOST SEVERE action across all disputes.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"severity order","quote":"Severity order (highest to lowest): 'close_and_reissue' > 'freeze_pending_investigation' > 'keep_active'.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"PIN lock cannot-unlock card with unauthorized transactions found is closed and replaced","quote":"If unauthorized transactions found: File dispute, close card, order replacement.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"clause":"each dispute keeps its own mapping","quote":"record each dispute's card_action based on its own category mapping (do NOT change individual dispute parameters)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"}]}},{"step":"alert_card_no_clear","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 003 clears the alert only when every transaction is confirmed, and the card follows the dispute mapping.","clauses":[{"clause":"do not clear the alert","kind":"kept","source":"Doc 003 'If they confirm all transactions are legitimate, clear the alert' says nothing for a denied transaction. The prohibition on the write stays."}]},{"step":"deferred_dispute_no_card_action","verdict":"rewrite","why":"Its rule that only filed disputes decide the card conflicts with doc 041 for a cannot-unlock PIN-locked card with a denied transaction.","clauses":[{"clause":"decide each card only from the disputes actually filed on it","kind":"unsupported","source":"Reading rule 3: doc 041 6.2 names the PIN lock cannot-unlock case and closes the card when unauthorized transactions are found, whether or not each was filed."},{"clause":"held back by another rule: do not say it can be filed later","kind":"kept","source":"Doc 031's pre-filing rules give no later route for such disputes. The clause holds back an offer that no passage makes."}],"rewrite":{"id":"deferred_dispute_no_card_action","by":"model","do":"A dispute that was held back sets no c